<code>assert index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>

This assert statement ensures that for every valid index less than the specified index, the element at that position either remains unchanged (if it was not null) or stays null (if it was originally null) after the removal operation.
--------------------
<code>assert index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>
